# The story, as the Tree tells it: once its roots held the six worlds apart, each on a branch of its own, and in every
# world's guardian it wove a root (the knot that held that world). The Rift split its trunk: the worlds fell onto one
# another and grew together at the seams, and the Tree is withering. The guardians, a root still woven in each, went mad
# and drink the last of its sap, and the seams tear under them. Each guardian that falls gives its root back: the Tree
# grows it along the seams and binds the world fast. The player is a dead man of an earlier expedition the Tree raised
# from his grave beneath it, to be its hands. It is old, proud and contemptuous; it needs him, and hates that it does.
